{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/960639-fallen","id":960639,"title":"Fallen?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-08-30T13:32:03-07:00","id":960639,"title":"Fallen?","content":"Just a quick setting question, when Mages say they live in a Fallen World, are they referring to the fact that they live in the phenomenal world rather than the noumenonal/supernal world, or the fact that the phenomenal world they live in is no longer as intimately connected with the noumenonal/supernal?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3326-an-fhuiseog","name":"An Fhuiseog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3326_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"271"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-30T13:37:20-07:00","id":960641,"title":"","content":"Technically the latter, but there's a bit of both really.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-30T15:09:56-07:00","id":960700,"title":"","content":"I like to interpret it that Fallen World is &quot;a child&quot; of Supernal/Phenomenal world, but chained by Exarchs into it's current shape.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-30T21:18:21-07:00","id":960854,"title":"","content":"Mostly the latter. The term phenomenal world is really more of an archmage's term than a normal mage's. In fact, I don't remember seeing it except in imperial mysteries.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7825-falcon777","name":"Falcon777","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-30T23:38:37-07:00","id":960915,"title":"","content":"The latter - there's always been a world that embodies the supernal, including the material realm, but with the Abyss between them that world is now Fallen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-01T22:32:29-07:00","id":962097,"title":"","content":"Even though Dave's given the answer just remember, every time you find something confusing in Mage's lore you've now got an excellent point for the people inside the setting to debate with one another. <br /> <br /> What if there are a group of Mages who believe that there shouldn't be a phenomenal world? What if they think that the way to defeat the Exarchs and ascend humanity is to utterly destroy the physical world and leave nothing but the Supernal realms remaining? What if that obscure and kinda weird group of academics who talked about that theory but no one ever took seriously suddenly resolved all their daily affairs and went to an archaeological dig in Peru?<br /> <br /> Instant story.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6748-michael-kenner","name":"Michael Kenner","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6748_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-02T08:15:37-07:00","id":962294,"title":"","content":"I had a NPC in my Chronicle who was fascinated by the magical pulse of &quot;whoa&quot; that went off during nuclear bombings in WW2 [described in Mage Noir, I think?]. He became obsessed with the idea that the way to destroy the Lie lies not in magic - which is outside the cage - but in cage itself, and that Sleepers have outgrown their jailers (he firmly believes that if Cold War went Hot, humanity would be saved) by finding a way to shatter building bars of the lie with, well, nuclear fission.<br /> He basically dreamed of a day world would get nuclear bombed into paradise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-02T08:42:41-07:00","id":962312,"title":"","content":"It's the basic ideology of the Cult of the Doomsday Clock.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-03T15:08:29-07:00","id":962982,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/960639-fallen?p=962294#post962294\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I had a NPC in my Chronicle who was fascinated by the magical pulse of &quot;whoa&quot; that went off during nuclear bombings in WW2 [described in Mage Noir, I think?]. He became obsessed with the idea that the way to destroy the Lie lies not in magic - which is outside the cage - but in cage itself, and that Sleepers have outgrown their jailers (he firmly believes that if Cold War went Hot, humanity would be saved) by finding a way to shatter building bars of the lie with, well, nuclear fission.<br /> He basically dreamed of a day world would get nuclear bombed into paradise.</div> </div> </div> </div>That would almost be a rational explanation of the other 2000 nuclear explosions we have had since WW2. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Trying to find a weakness in the cage.<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_nuclear_weapons_tests\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0b/Radiation_warning_symbol.svg/1280px-Radiation_warning_symbol.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=index&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_nuclear_weapons_tests\" target=\"_blank\"> List of nuclear weapons tests - Wikipedia </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_nuclear_weapons_tests\" target=\"_blank\"> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_nuclear_weapons_tests </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=LLCF7vPanrY\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=LLCF7vPanrY\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=LLCF7vPanrY\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=LLCF7vPanrY </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2839-lundgren","name":"Lundgren","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T13:52:19-07:00","id":965249,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/960639-fallen?p=960915#post960915\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The latter - there's always been a world that embodies the supernal, including the material realm, but with the Abyss between them that world is now Fallen.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks that's as clear as it gets! I know it's fairly obvious from the core, but I wasn't 100% sure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3326-an-fhuiseog","name":"An Fhuiseog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3326_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"271"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T19:18:17-07:00","id":965419,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>An Fhuiseog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/960639-fallen?p=965249#post965249\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks that's as clear as it gets! I know it's fairly obvious from the core, but I wasn't 100% sure.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly I wasn't entirely clear on that myself until I saw Dave's reply. It's always been my assumption, but I wasn't 100% sure either.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6748-michael-kenner","name":"Michael Kenner","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6748_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}